  /* ===== ISLE part 2i (v36): the street play at Okachimachi =====
     The title's free walk becomes an open-world street game in the manner of the big city sandboxes (the genre's controls and rules, none of
     any one game's assets): on foot (move, sprint, jump, punch), into a car on the street and out again, a wanted level that rises with every
     offence and falls when the police lose sight of you, officers on foot and a patrol car, and an arrest that ends at the police box. While she
     is wanted, Luna's eyes are hidden behind a mosaic, as faces are on the news. Everything people say reaches her phone, in a messenger of its
     own design. An original quiet man of the back streets, 影山, points her to an original diner under the tracks, 食堂ともしび, where the master
     listens. No firearms and nobody is killed: the people knocked down get up again. */
